Usage:
  nucleus completion <shell>

Print a completion script for one shell, generated from the command table, the Django-style aliases, each command's flags and its grammar (the subcommands a first argument accepts, the values a flag accepts), so a word the completion offers is a word the binary accepts.

Arguments:
  <shell>  One of bash, zsh, fish

Shells:
  bash  Source the output, or install it under bash-completion's completions directory
  zsh   Write the output to a file named _nucleus on your fpath, then run compinit
  fish  Write the output to ~/.config/fish/completions/nucleus.fish

Examples:
  nucleus completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/nucleus
  nucleus completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_nucleus"
  nucleus completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/nucleus.fish

The script is a snapshot of this binary: regenerate it after upgrading the CLI.
